1
00:00:00,190 --> 00:00:03,160
Why is a wind-turbine maker building

2
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:05,080
an AI data centre?

3
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,800
In Inner Mongolia, Envision is connecting

4
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,800
those businesses through an AI campus

5
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,080
called Galaxy.

6
00:00:11,190 --> 00:00:13,700
Follow the electricity to understand why

7
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:15,780
an energy company wants to build

8
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,080
it.

9
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:18,550
Envision founder and CEO Lei Zhang

10
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:21,830
started the company in 2007, making

11
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:23,000
wind turbines.

12
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,260
It expanded into batteries and energy

13
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:26,080
systems.

14
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:29,080
Computing creates demand for that equipment.

15
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:32,040
Ulanqab sits about 300 kilometres northwest

16
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:35,080
of Beijing, in China's Inner Mongolia.

17
00:00:35,190 --> 00:00:39,020
SemiAnalysis visited in September 2026.

18
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:40,330
Its report is the starting point

19
00:00:40,330 --> 00:00:41,080
for this story.

20
00:00:41,190 --> 00:00:45,010
OpenAI's Stargate is the American comparison.

21
00:00:45,010 --> 00:00:48,080
Galaxy is a separate Envision project.

22
00:00:48,190 --> 00:00:51,280
SemiAnalysis reports 120 megawatts delivered in

23
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:54,080
August 2026, within a year.

24
00:00:54,190 --> 00:00:57,080
That's power for computing equipment.

25
00:00:57,190 --> 00:00:59,890
Megawatts measure the rate of electricity

26
00:00:59,990 --> 00:01:02,080
use, not AI performance.

27
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:05,080
The full plan is 800 megawatts.

28
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:07,550
Used continuously, that matches the annual

29
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:11,360
grid electricity bought by about 650,000

30
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:12,000
US homes.

31
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,890
Or about 67 stadiums like Munich's

32
00:01:14,990 --> 00:01:18,530
Allianz Arena, comparing their maximum available

33
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:20,080
electrical power.

34
00:01:20,190 --> 00:01:22,500
For AI, imagine eight centres using

35
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:25,080
100 megawatts for computing each.

36
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:27,000
Cooling needs extra power.

37
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,080
These are comparisons, not measured usage.

38
00:01:30,190 --> 00:01:33,310
Accelerators process data, with memory and

39
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:36,080
networks keeping them supplied.

40
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:38,000
Power must reach those racks reliably.

41
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,850
Their heat also has to leave

42
00:01:39,850 --> 00:01:41,080
the building.

43
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:44,160
SemiAnalysis describes a five-megawatt pilot testing

44
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:46,330
a different way of supplying the

45
00:01:46,330 --> 00:01:47,080
racks.

46
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:51,090
Solid-state transformers convert incoming alternating current

47
00:01:51,090 --> 00:01:54,000
into an 800-volt direct-current bus.

48
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
At the same power, doubling DC

49
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,980
voltage halves the current in a

50
00:01:57,980 --> 00:01:59,000
conductor.

51
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,330
At the same resistance, lower current

52
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:03,060
reduces heating losses.

53
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:06,080
Galaxy's actual savings need measuring.

54
00:02:06,190 --> 00:02:08,770
Rack electronics still reduce voltage further

55
00:02:08,770 --> 00:02:11,080
before that power reaches the chips.

56
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:13,890
Envision also makes turbines and batteries,

57
00:02:13,990 --> 00:02:16,190
extending its role beyond owning the

58
00:02:16,330 --> 00:02:17,080
building.

59
00:02:17,190 --> 00:02:20,380
The company can coordinate generation, storage

60
00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:23,200
and equipment supplying power inside the

61
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:24,080
campus.

62
00:02:24,190 --> 00:02:25,750
But a wind farm's rated power

63
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:27,280
is not its output at every

64
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,060
moment.

65
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:30,000
The wind rises and falls.

66
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,930
Computing equipment needs reliable power through

67
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:34,070
those changes.

68
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:36,890
Batteries store some surplus electricity and

69
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:39,330
supply it when generation falls below

70
00:02:39,330 --> 00:02:40,080
demand.

71
00:02:40,190 --> 00:02:43,230
Their usefulness depends on power, stored

72
00:02:43,230 --> 00:02:45,330
energy, and how long the calm

73
00:02:45,330 --> 00:02:46,080
lasts.

74
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:48,440
'Wind-powered' does not establish that wind

75
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:51,080
supplies all the electricity, every hour.

76
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,550
How much of Galaxy is fitted

77
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:55,040
with hardware and actually running remains

78
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:56,080
unverified.

79
00:02:56,190 --> 00:02:58,550
Reported delivered capacity is not a

80
00:02:58,550 --> 00:03:01,170
measurement of load drawn by working

81
00:03:01,330 --> 00:03:02,080
servers.

82
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:04,630
Buildings and megawatts cannot confirm installed

83
00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:06,200
chips, or how much work they

84
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,080
produce.

85
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:10,170
Envision's larger capacity announcements also need

86
00:03:10,170 --> 00:03:13,260
reconciling with SemiAnalysis's description of the

87
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,080
campus.

88
00:03:14,190 --> 00:03:15,770
Those are questions for Zhang and

89
00:03:15,770 --> 00:03:18,190
the site's engineers, alongside the wider

90
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:19,080
strategy.

91
00:03:19,190 --> 00:03:20,540
The next test is how much

92
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:23,150
useful computing this energy system can

93
00:03:23,150 --> 00:03:23,320
deliver.
